  "notes": "COMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {孤立|こりつ}する: to become isolated\n- {孤立|こりつ}を{深|ふか}める: to become increasingly isolated\n- {孤立|こりつ}{無援|むえん}: isolated and helpless (four-character compound)\n- {社会的|しゃかいてき}{孤立|こりつ}: social isolation\n- {国際的|こくさいてき}に{孤立|こりつ}する: to be internationally isolated\n\nUSAGE:\nUsed across many contexts: social isolation of individuals, physical isolation of areas cut off by disasters, and diplomatic isolation of nations. The word carries a sense of vulnerability — being alone without support.\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n{孤立|こりつ} vs {孤独|こどく}: {孤独|こどく} (loneliness, solitude) focuses on the emotional experience of being alone. {孤立|こりつ} emphasizes the objective state of being separated or cut off from a group, whether one feels lonely or not.",
